(a) This permit is allowed with conditions in all zoning districts. Whenever a permit is sought for activities in primarily residential neighborhoods, extra consideration shall be given to the conditions imposed to ameliorate as much as possible inconvenience to the residents.
(b) General standards. Prior to making application for a permit, it shall be incumbent on the applicant to meet with the director of community development, sheriff and director of public safety, or their designees, to review locations and the general scope of activities planned during the production. A copy of the script shall be made available, upon request, to allow the county staff to better understand the applicant's needs. The following general standards shall apply to all permits:
